It's a good sign that our products are in demand and more marketable.
Organic rice production differs from conventional rice production in that it requires farmers to avoid the use of chemical fertilizers and pesticides, and all production processes from start to finish must be done with Proper rules that pass the inspection and have a clear certificate.
Nep Ang, an organic rice farmer in Trapeang Koh village, Trapeang Tbong commune, Tram Kak district, Takeo province, has been producing organic rice since 2007 and has so far grown three hectares of organic rice.
He claims that producing organic rice allows him to pay lower production costs than using chemical fertilizers and get higher sales prices.
It will encourage farmers to continue to produce more organic rice.
