Farmer Nep Ang, who also represents organic rice farmers in Trapeang Tbong commune, said that organic rice farmers in his community could produce about 1,000 tonnes of organic rice a year, but CEDAC could only afford 300 tonnes. Therefore, farmers have to sell the remaining produce to other traders at normal prices.
