According to Hsu, after a two-week stock price survey, almost 3.36 million shares were sold.
He said more than 90 per cent of those shares were of interest to foreign investors.
The Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia (SECC) yesterday issued a statement instructing the public to be more vigilant against fraudulent high-yield investment lobbying by a number of unlicensed companies.
Joint ventures raise capital from the public to invest in a specific project and provide investors with a realistic level of business profit.
The Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, which has the role of managing and overseeing all activities related to the securities sector in Cambodia, has issued a statement stating that the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia has not yet given permission or license to any company to do this type of business. The regulator is currently studying other risks.
Sieng Thirith, director of the Legal Affairs Department of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, told the Post yesterday that some companies were now operating illegally in joint ventures and networks that the public could face. With fraud, serious losses.
In recent days, the US Securities and Exchange Commission has filed a lawsuit against TelexFree, which is known for its online revenue, for embezzling $ 1.1 billion from investors around the world.
He said he always told everyone in advance about the irregularities of such investments and the fact that the company was not properly licensed.
