Minister urges more green energy industry
The Minister of Industry and Handicrafts has urged the implementation of green industry among local industrialists and artisans to achieve sustainable development and economic growth.
Cham Prasidh said this at a seminar on green industry yesterday.
The Green Industry Workshop is designed to educate manufacturers and artisans about renewable energy, clean energy, clean production and energy efficiency in order to reduce dependence on fossil fuels and inclusiveness. In the prevention of climate change.
