Visits to Preah Vihear increase, but accommodation is limited
Preah Vihear: Data from the provincial tourism department shows that the number of tourists visiting Preah Vihear province increased in early 2014.
However, accommodation in the province is still limited as most visitors return to Siem Reap.
The total number of tourists visiting Preah Vihear was 61,671 from January to March, according to the data.
There were 13,217 foreign visitors, an increase of about 77 per cent from the same period last year, while the number of national visitors was 48,454, an increase of 40 per cent.
You Sokha, deputy director of the Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Tourism, told the Post yesterday that the number of tourists visiting the province was increasing year by year, but most visitors only took the area as a transit point. After spending the day visiting the Preah Vihear temple.
The guests did not stay in the surrounding area or in Preah Vihear province, as they often left in the evening to stay in Siem Reap after the road connecting the two provinces was built and made it easier to travel.
He said that the temples of Preah Vihear and Siem Reap were more than 200 kilometers apart, and that in the past, travel between the two provinces had been difficult due to road problems.
The national road from Preah Vihear to Siem Reap was completed and put into operation in 2012, making it easy for people to travel in just over three hours.
To date, the entire province of Preah Vihear has 12 resorts and restaurants, 10 entertainment venues, 2 hotels and 27 guesthouses, most of which are concentrated in Saem commune of Choam Ksan district, about 20 km from the Preah Vihear temple.
Vuth Dara, owner of the Preah Vihear Heritage Guesthouse, which has 30 rooms and is about 15 kilometers from the Preah Vihear temple, said the number of guesthouses in his commune has increased significantly in recent years, with the number of rooms increasing. Up to nearly 500 rooms.
Investors expect high demand for accommodation services, which will make them interested in investing in guesthouse construction.
