The number of tourists visiting Siem Reap in the next three to four days of the upcoming Khmer New Year will increase to more than 200,000, an approximate number of tourists per month due to the Angkor Sankranti event.
The increase in tourists will increase demand for accommodation services, as some innkeepers and hoteliers said yesterday that bookings during the Khmer New Year are beginning to take shape. Gradual increase.
