Ly Sam Eng has been renting an apartment on Sothearos Street near the Russian Embassy in Cambodia for $ 420 a month for almost three years now.
Since the beginning of 2010, Sam Eng has used this location as a place to serve as a decoration service for rituals, ceremonies and other traditional ceremonies.
But from next month, Sam Eng will not be able to continue doing business here as the lease expires and the rent has risen sharply.
The 33-year-old told the Post on Monday:
Ms. Sam Eng pointed to the Japanese Aeon Mall located in front of the house and continued:
She said the sub-tenants would renovate the location into a bank or business office.
Currently, residential and commercial buildings along Sothearos Blvd., between Wat Svay Po Pe, the Russian Embassy in Cambodia and the Chamkarmon traffic light, are mostly family businesses.
It is a place for ordinary homes, grocery stores, rattan shops for home decoration, and especially a stretch of road with a massage parlor worth 10,000 riel in a row.
