The Cambodian Ministry of Commerce will meet with a group of rice traders on Wednesday to discuss the establishment of the Cambodian Rice Federation, a national institution for government partners in industrial development.
The formation of the federation follows the approval of Prime Minister Hun Sen, who on Tuesday last week decided to allow the establishment of a rice-rice federation to facilitate cooperation with rice federations from other countries. In the ASEAN region and to prepare to compete in the ASEAN Economic Community in 2015.
Representatives of the Cambodian Rice Traders, who now have separate groups, said the establishment of a national joint federation was necessary to strengthen cooperation among traders as previous missions took place. Separate.
David Van Vichet, deputy secretary general of the Cambodian Rice Producers and Exporters Coalition, said the establishment of a national federation was a step forward in creating an environment for all traders to work together better. Common interests.
Cambodia, which exported nearly 400,000 tonnes of rice last year, has at least three major rice associations.
The Cambodian Rice Exporters Association, chaired by Lim Bunheng, is chaired by David Van Vichet, the Cambodian Rice Producers and Exporters Coalition, and the Cambodian Rice Exporters Federation, chaired by Kim Savuth.
The presence of divisive associations in the past seems to make each group of traders do not cooperate well.
When Cambodian rice was selected as the world's second-best rice last year, some rice exporters claimed through local media that the achievement belonged to them.
The announcement of the companies is a departure from the pre-departure agreement, while representatives of the federation and the company both agree that they represent Cambodian rice, and all the successes are the reputation and achievements of the company. Cambodia.
