Phnom Penh: Toll Royal, a train carrier, installed a scanner at its dry port yesterday and began inspections today, a positive development to keep costs down. On time and cost of transport on the train more competitive.
If there is no scanner at the dry port located on the western outskirts of Phnom Penh, cargo in containers transported by train from Phnom Penh to Sihanoukville International Port must enter the scanner at Sihanoukville Port.
This requires the transfer of the container from the carriage to the truck upon arrival at the port to enter the scanner, then the transfer from the truck to another port for transfer to the ship, which is a procedure that causes inconvenience. Complicated, time consuming and costly.
David Kerr, chief executive of Toll Royal, told the Post yesterday that the lack of scanners in the dry port in the past had made the process of transporting trains expensive and time consuming.
Therefore, Toll Royal decided to install a scanner at the dry port, which is located on the outskirts of Phnom Penh, and has a Camcontrol official to inspect before shipping the goods to the port.
He said Toll would make it easier for exporters by reducing road congestion and lowering shipping costs.
The company first started shipping in late 2010, but then imported only imported goods such as cement, fuel and coal.
It was not until August 2013 that the company began transporting rice from Phnom Penh to Sihanoukville for the first time.
So far, the company has been able to transport about 17 million liters of fuel and about 9,000 tons of cement monthly from Sihanoukville port to Phnom Penh dry port and about 9,000 tons of coal monthly from Sihanoukville to the district. Touk Meas, Kampot province as well.
The company is also seeing an increase in shipments from Phnom Penh to the port, such as rice, linen and garments, which now total more than 1,600 containers a month.
Kim Savuth, director general of Khmer Food Rice Exporters, which has a factory in Phnom Penh and president of the Cambodian Rice Exporters Federation, said the installation and operation of scanners at the dry port along the railway was a positive development. Responding to the request of the Federation of Rice Exporters since 2012.
Freight by train from the dry port on the outskirts of Phnom Penh to the port of Sihanoukville costs $ 120 per container, while freight by truck costs $ 190 per container.
So Nguon, CEO of So Nguon Group, which has a number of commercial companies, including trucking companies, said the installation of scanners along the railway would improve the efficiency of rail freight services. And enable exporters to reduce their reliance on trucking.
Sokha Hotel Phnom Penh could be opened as a casino
The $ 100 million Sokha Phnom Penh Hotel, which is still under construction in Chroy Changvar, will open as a casino in the future if licensed.
Sve Vuthy, head of legal and affairs affairs at Sokimex, the parent company of Sokha Hotel, yesterday confirmed that the company was considering opening a casino at the hotel.
Sokha Hotel currently operates a casino at Phnom Thansur Bokor Resort.
The claim came after a Post reporter went to a 14-hectare site in front of the Royal Palace, where a staff member in charge of site planning indicated that the hotel's ground floor had been demolished. Signed for casinos and gambling rooms.
But Wutty dismissed the engineer's comments, saying without elaborating that the ground floor was intended for entertainment purposes only.
We have no plans for gambling or casinos because we do not have a license.
He said Sokimex had not yet applied to the Ministry of Economy and Finance for a license.
But Sokha Hotel's future plans are likely to wait at least another 20 years, as Nagaworld, the only casino operator in Phnom Penh, has been given a monopoly on gambling operations in Phnom Penh until 2035.
Chrun Therawat, head of casino management at the Ministry of Economy and Finance, said he had not received any information about Sokha Hotel's desire to open a casino.
He said that under Cambodian gambling law, the government would not allow gambling in the city or in Siem Reap, a high tourist destination.
But if there is any decision from the government, we as a technical team will monitor and find a solution.
Vuthy says the company hopes to expand the hotel from its current 16 floors to 30.
In the short term, the opening date of the Sokha Phnom Penh Hotel has been postponed again, although construction is ongoing and the entire exterior structure is now complete.
Vuthy said he now intends to launch a test run in October this year, and that the entire process could be completed by mid-2015.
The completion date was originally scheduled for early 2012, after construction began in 2009.
Vuthy says he is putting pressure on contractors to speed up completion by the new deadline.
Cambodian tax experts and officials have agreed to assist the United States in its efforts to crack down on tax evasion in collaboration with local banks to provide financial data on Americans' citizenship and trade abroad.
Speaking at the 17th Private Sector Government Forum on Tuesday, Prime Minister Hun Sen affirmed the government's intention to assist the United States with the new US FATCA tax law, which will take effect on July 1.
The Internal Revenue Service (IRS), a U.S. tax collection agency, estimates $ 100 billion in annual tax losses from overseas bank accounts.
Although FATCA specializes in tracking tax evaders for at least $ 50,000, every American with a bank account in Cambodia and many other countries will face additional levels of scrutiny.
The measure also looks at dividends, stocks, insurance information, investments and other relevant financial data made by foreign financial institutions FFI.
Mr. In Channy, General Manager of ACLEDA Bank explained:
Cambodia, along with other participating countries, will submit its first financial information list for the 2014 period in March 2015.
The new tax law for overseas Americans was signed in 2010, with the first date for all countries in January 2013.
But Channy said the law was likely to violate Cambodia's legal sovereignty and called on the government to discuss it with the IRS.
Companies can provide information independently, or they can agree that the bank can make an agreement with the government directly, then contact the United States.
Cambodia has not yet chosen these means.
As President of the Bank and the Financial Sector Working Group, Channy said that compliance with Cambodia's FATCA would work better through the government than with the volunteering of private companies and reporting financial information independently. To the IRS.
The US Embassy did not respond to requests for comment regarding the size of the US expat community in Cambodia.
