The government will continue to ease the tax burden on investment companies, but at the same time the private sector must continue to work to build and develop its capacity and abandon the practice of seeking tax incentives from the state instead of providing information. And recommendations to the Royal Government, especially in addressing the challenges and seizing the opportunities arising from the ASEAN Economic Integration 2015.
However, the 17th forum has not yet addressed all the issues raised by the working group, with Prime Minister Hun Sen asserting that The issue that is not being resolved at this time will require the working group from the 10 private sectors to meet with the chairperson of the working group, which is composed of ministers representing each ministry.
Customs revenue rises after government action
Phnom Penh: Prime Minister Hun Sen says monthly customs revenue collection has increased by more than $ 20 million since November 2013 after the government ordered the General Department of Customs and Excise to strengthen the efficiency of tax collection to increase National income.
Speaking at the 17th Royal Government Private Sector Forum at the Peace Palace on Tuesday, Mr. Hun Sen said that since November last year, the average monthly customs revenue has increased significantly. Compared to the average monthly rate in 2013.
According to the Prime Minister, while the average monthly tax collection rate last year was around 330 billion riels per month, about $ 82.5 million, customs revenue increased to 365 billion riels in November and so on. Increased to 439 billion riel in December, about $ 109 million.
In January 2014, revenue from customs duties increased to 437 billion riels, while revenue from customs duties in February was 416 billion riels.
He said the government did not increase tariffs on imported goods, except for some health-related goods such as cigarettes and alcohol.
The government has given the customs 60 days to adjust its work.
