But he said the reforms seemed a bit slow as Cambodia would become a member of the ASEAN Economic Community in 2015, allowing for a free flow of goods from countries in the region duty-free.
Son Chhay, a CNRP-elected lawmaker, criticized the tax collection in the past for contracting, causing hundreds of millions of dollars in lost national currency each year.
He said Cambodia needed to further strengthen its tax collection, as customs revenue would soon be gone after Cambodia joined the ASEAN Economic Community.
