Investors are considering skills and costs for workers' salaries.
It is not possible to increase the salary too much, which causes factories to run away from Cambodia.
He said the Ministry of Commerce already had plans to attract investors.
But we need to consider our sharp competitors, such as Myanmar, Laos and Bangladesh.
Figures from the Ministry of Commerce show total exports of textile products were $ 5.5 billion in 2013, up 20 percent from 2012.
Textiles account for 80 percent of Cambodia's total exports.
