The transaction allows international callers to completely avoid sending calls to licensed international operators, which charge a standard 4 cents per minute connection fee for international calls.
The Sim box charges a lower connection fee of about 2 cents per minute to international callers before forwarding the call via a local SIM card is almost free.
According to Telecom Cambodia and industry regulators, the result that callers and receivers are unaware of is poor quality calls, which have been common in Cambodia since April last year.
