Phnom Penh: The Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) in Cambodia has provided a grant of $ 11.5 million to Cambodia through the Ministry of Mines and Energy to build and rehabilitate a small hydropower plant in Ratanakkiri province that could provide electricity. Total 1,225 kW.
The small-scale construction and rehabilitation site officially opened last weekend, presided over by Mr. Ith Prang, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Mines and Energy, a representative of the Embassy of Japan and a representative of JICA in Cambodia.
The project is expected to be completed in March 2015.
Speaking at the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction and rehabilitation of a small hydropower plant in Banlung City, Ratanakkiri Province on Saturday, January 25, Mr. Ith Prang said that through this project, the people of Banlung and surrounding areas will receive a full supply of electricity. More stability will benefit about 18,000 families living in the area.
The scale of this small-scale hydropower construction and rehabilitation project is divided into three sub-projects: first, the construction of the first round 265 kW hydropower plant, and second, the restoration of the existing second round hydropower plant. 960 kilowatts of power and thirdly, the construction of a 22 kilovolt sub-transmission line with a length of 730 meters.
The first and second projects will start construction at the same time, while the third project will have to wait until the first two projects are completed.
